{"aggregate_id": "01M2TKC7K6JBT3W7RGDZC7SNV1", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M2TKC7M0DM5P5VCJDBPWVTF7", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-09-18T15:50:17.974682+00:00", "friendly_name": "Decide the fate of out-of-matrix test directories", "mission_id": "01M2TKC7K6JBT3W7RGDZC7SNV1", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "decide-out-of-matrix-test-dirs-01M2TKC7", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Issue #4369 made every un-lane'd test directory visible in the CI module registry but explicitly deferred deciding what to do about them. This mission closes that decision debt: for each secondary test tree, it either promotes the tree into a CI lane (backed by a measured timing run) or records a sharpened reason explaining why an existing gate already covers it. The outcome is a registry whose out-of-matrix entries are decisions, not snapshots, protecting the project from regressions that would otherwise persist unseen on the main branch.", "purpose_tldr": "Turn the recorded out-of-matrix test-directory inventory from a passive snapshot into deliberate, evidence-backed CI coverage decisions so no test tree is silently unrun on main.", "target_branch": "chore/decide-out-of-matrix-test-dirs", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-09-18T15:50:17.984193+00:00"}
